        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>You check range from the Origin. For a Vertex Area Attack, you choose the origin as you would for any standard Area Attack. Then you choose two other adjacent hexes touching a vertex of the origin. There&#39;s your area. On level ground, the range to the other two hexes is 1, but elevation could change that.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Unless something changed in the final rules. I&#39;ll confess I don&#39;t have the printed rulebook in front of me.</p>",
